# Musizeer — the variables of docker-compose.yaml. Copy this file to `.env` next to it (never commit `.env`).
# The guide, with the commands that generate each secret: docs/deployment.md, which also has the reference table of
# every variable (old name, new name, meaning, default). The names of the variables before Musizeer (AUTH_SECRET,
# CREDENTIALS_KEY, PUBLIC_URL, APP_PORT, ...) are NOT read any more: a process that finds one says which name replaces
# it, and compose refuses to start without the required ones under their new names.
#
# The groups below: required / address / database / images / advanced.

# ===== Required (no default: compose refuses to start without them) =====

# The database password. Letters and digits: it goes into a URL (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 24`).
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# MUSIZEER_AUTH_SECRET firma i token di sessione (docs/permissions.md). NON va nel repository: scrivila qui, in .env.
# Con l'autenticazione attiva l'app rifiuta di partire se è vuota, più corta di 32 caratteri o un segnaposto
# (change-me-in-production, change-me, secret): chi la conosce può falsificare il token di un amministratore.
# Un valore lungo e casuale, generato così:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Cambiarla fa uscire tutti: ognuno dovrà accedere di nuovo.
# MUSIZEER_AUTH_SECRET=

# MUSIZEER_CREDENTIALS_KEY cifra tutto ciò che Musizeer conserva per collegarsi ai servizi (docs/credentials.md):
# token OAuth2, login, API key, client OAuth, token delle sorgenti e impostazioni segrete. NON va nel repository:
# scrivila qui, in .env. L'app e i worker rifiutano di partire se manca, è vuota o non è una chiave valida. Una chiave
# Fernet (44 caratteri), generata UNA volta così:
#   docker run --rm musizeer-app python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
# (compose non costruisce nulla senza la chiave: la stessa chiave si ottiene con
#   openssl rand -base64 32 | tr '+/' '-_'
# che dà la base64 urlsafe di 32 byte casuali, cioè una chiave Fernet valida.)
# CONSERVALA con i backup del database (insieme a questo .env): senza la chiave le credenziali salvate non si possono
# più leggere e ogni account va ricollegato. Non cambiarla a mano: per sostituirla vedi "Rotazione".
# MUSIZEER_CREDENTIALS_KEY=
#
# Rotazione: la nuova chiave diventa MUSIZEER_CREDENTIALS_KEY, la vecchia va qui (più chiavi separate da virgole), poi
# `python -m scripts.rotate_credentials_key --apply` ricifra tutto; infine si toglie la vecchia da questa riga.
# MUSIZEER_CREDENTIALS_KEY_PREVIOUS=

# The first administrator, created at the first start while there are no users.
# MUSIZEER_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL=you@example.org
# MUSIZEER_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=

# ===== Address (docs/deployment.md, "The public URL") =====

# The address your users type in the browser, with no trailing slash:
#   http://192.168.1.20:8080   https://music.example.org   http://my-server.my-tailnet.ts.net
# OAuth2 providers send the browser back to "<MUSIZEER_PUBLIC_URL>/api/auth/<provider>/callback" (the redirect URI to
# register at the service) and the sign-in ends on MUSIZEER_PUBLIC_URL, so it must be the address as the BROWSER sees
# it. Default http://localhost, which is right only on the machine that runs the stack and only on port 80 (set it when
# MUSIZEER_PORT is not 80).
# MUSIZEER_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost

# The port the web app is published on (host side). Default 80.
# MUSIZEER_PORT=80

# Only when the two differ from what MUSIZEER_PUBLIC_URL gives (a proxy that does not forward /api, say):
#   MUSIZEER_APP_BASE_URL   the base of the OAuth2 callback, default "<MUSIZEER_PUBLIC_URL>/api"
#   MUSIZEER_FRONTEND_URL   where the browser is sent when a sign-in ends, default MUSIZEER_PUBLIC_URL
# MUSIZEER_APP_BASE_URL=
# MUSIZEER_FRONTEND_URL=

# Where the web app's nginx reaches the API: scheme://host:port, no path. Default http://app:8000, the `app` service of
# docker-compose.yaml; change it only if you renamed that service or run the API elsewhere. nginx looks the name up again
# every few seconds, so a recreated API container is found. The name server it asks: MUSIZEER_DNS_RESOLVER (default
# 127.0.0.11, Docker's own).
# MUSIZEER_BACKEND_URL=http://app:8000
# MUSIZEER_DNS_RESOLVER=127.0.0.11

# The prefix the browser reaches the API with, applied to the cover, preview and stream URLs (default /api), and the
# origins CORS allows, separated by commas (default *).
# MUSIZEER_PUBLIC_API_PREFIX=/api
# MUSIZEER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=*

# ===== Database (docs/postgresql.md) =====

# I file docker-compose girano su PostgreSQL: POSTGRES_PASSWORD è sopra. Di solito non servono, i default sono questi.
# POSTGRES_USER=musizeer
# POSTGRES_DB=musizeer
#
# DATABASE_URL: dove sono i dati. Compose lo costruisce dalle tre variabili qui sopra; fuori da compose si imposta a
# mano. Non impostata: SQLite, il file MUSIZEER_DATA_DIR/musizeer.db.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://musizeer:password@postgres:5432/musizeer
#
# Redis, il broker di Celery e il canale dei progressi (default: il servizio `redis` di compose).
# REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0
#
# Quanto (ms) una scrittura aspetta il lock di un'altra prima di rispondere 503 database_busy (default 15000):
# busy timeout di SQLite, lock_timeout di PostgreSQL. API e worker condividono il DB.
# MUSIZEER_DB_BUSY_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
# PostgreSQL: una query oltre questo tempo (ms) viene interrotta (default 120000, 0 = mai).
# MUSIZEER_DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# PostgreSQL: connessioni per processo (API e ogni worker; default 5 + 10 di overflow). max_connections del server
# deve coprire la somma.
# MUSIZEER_DB_POOL_SIZE=5
# MUSIZEER_DB_MAX_OVERFLOW=10
#
# Backup before a migration (docs/migrations.md): when `init` has migrations to apply it first dumps the database into
# /data/backups (volume `data`) and keeps the last MUSIZEER_MIGRATION_BACKUPS_KEEP (default 5). A failed backup stops the
# migration. MUSIZEER_MIGRATION_BACKUP=off skips it, for whoever backs the database up otherwise.
# MUSIZEER_MIGRATION_BACKUPS_KEEP=5
# MUSIZEER_MIGRATION_BACKUP=on

# ===== Images (docker-compose.yaml) =====

# docker-compose.yaml usa le immagini pubblicate su GHCR (linux/amd64 e linux/arm64). Senza MUSIZEER_VERSION prende
# :latest, cioè l'ultimo merge su master; con una versione (i tag delle release GitHub, senza la "v") resta su quella
# finché non la cambi. Dopo averla cambiata: docker compose pull && docker compose up -d
# MUSIZEER_VERSION=1.2.0
# Un altro registry o proprietario (un fork):
# MUSIZEER_IMAGES=ghcr.io/sossiogll
# Il repository GitHub delle cui release il controllo degli aggiornamenti si fida (un fork indica il suo):
# MUSIZEER_UPDATE_REPOSITORY=sossiogll/musizeer
# Per costruire le immagini dal sorgente invece di scaricarle:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml -f docker-compose.build.yml up -d --build

# ===== Advanced =====

# --- Folders (docs/deployment.md, "Folders") ---
# There is NO folder variable. The folders are declared in the interface (Administration > Root folders: the root
# folders, and the working folder and the library folder as settings over them) and the host tells the gateway. What
# you do here is MOUNT: compose mounts the `downloads` volume at /downloads in the app, the workers and the gateway, and
# the `library` volume at /library in the gateway only. To use a folder of the host, mount it in a
# docker-compose.override.yml (the library in the gateway; the downloads folder in the app, the workers and the gateway,
# at the same path) and declare it in the interface. Mount only the music folders into the gateway: what you mount is
# what an administrator can declare.

# --- Provider gateway (docs/gateway.md) ---
# The seccomp profile of the gateway container, a file on the machine that runs Docker. Default: the one in a clone of
# the repository. Installing from the files of a release, they sit side by side and this is
# ./musizeer-gateway.seccomp.json already (the release's docker-compose.yaml says so).
# MUSIZEER_GATEWAY_SECCOMP_PROFILE=./gateway/seccomp/musizeer-gateway.json
#
# The most processes and threads the gateway container may hold, the gateway and every provider's sandbox together (the
# container's pids limit: nothing outside the container counts toward it, so a busy host does not matter). Each sandbox
# is also held to the `limits.processes` of its provider's manifest (default 512, at most 1024) by the gateway.
# MUSIZEER_GATEWAY_PIDS_LIMIT=4096
#
# The most any provider may be given, whatever its manifest asks (defaults: 2048 MB, 4096 open files, 1024 processes).
# MUSIZEER_GATEWAY_MAX_MEMORY_MB=2048
# MUSIZEER_GATEWAY_MAX_OPEN_FILES=4096
# MUSIZEER_GATEWAY_MAX_PROCESSES=1024

# --- Development stack (docker-compose.dev.yml only) ---
# The staging folder (mounted as /downloads in the application, the workers and the gateway) and the library (mounted as
# /library in the gateway), and the ports of the Vite dev server and of the local OCI registry.
# MUSIZEER_DOWNLOADS_DIR=./data/downloads
# MUSIZEER_LIBRARY_DIR=./data/library
# MUSIZEER_DEV_FRONTEND_PORT=3000
# MUSIZEER_DEV_OCI_REGISTRY_PORT=15000
